    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747-a2">

                <pb facs="1200" n="1104" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1104"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Exhibit</hi> A.—J. G., Jr.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Puerto Cabello, Venezuela</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 9, 1870</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your own satisfaction, as well as for
                    the information of whom it may concern, I beg to state that during the time I
                    commanded the steamer Virginius she violated no law or custom of commerce, and
                    never exhibited any other than the American flag; that she cleared and entered
                    regularly at each port, and, so far as I know, she is intended as nothing else
                    than an ordinary merchant-vessel.</p>
                <p>Yours, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. E. SHEPPERD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Dr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Lacombe</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >United States Consul, Puerto Cabello.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
